course: dictionary
lesson: 7882
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A ramp can be a thing you walk or roll up and down, or a verb meaning to increase. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning is used. «The lever, the wheel and axle, the pulley and the ramp are simple machines.» Here a ramp is a thing: a sloping surface that joins a low place and a high place.
explain: When ramp is a verb, it means increase. «Ramp up the speed» means make the speed go up. Check by swapping in your meaning: "increase the speed" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Workers cut stone blocks with copper tools, dragged them on sledges over sand wetted to make it slippery, and moved them up ramps.» The words moved them up tell you the ramps were sloping surfaces that people climbed with heavy stones.
fact: A ramp is a sloping surface that joins a lower place and a higher place, used instead of steps.
fact: «Ramp up» means increase, as in «ramp up the speed».
fact: A ramp is a simple machine: it makes lifting easier by spreading the work over a longer distance.
fact: «Blocking ramps, lifts and wide parking spaces can stop people with disabilities getting where they need to go.»
fact: When you meet a word with two meanings, try each one in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
exercise: «The lever, the wheel and axle, the pulley and the ramp are simple machines.» In this sentence, what is a ramp? | A small pond full of frogs | *A sloping surface that joins a low place and a high place | A loud noise made by a machine | A type of hat worn by workers
exercise: Mum says, «Let's ramp up the speed on the bike.» What does ramp up mean? | *Increase | Make it slower | Clean the bike | Stop the bike
exercise: «Workers cut stone blocks with copper tools, dragged them on sledges over sand wetted to make it slippery, and moved them up ramps.» Find and copy the word that means made wet. | copper | *wetted | sand | dragged
test: «Blocking ramps, lifts and wide parking spaces can stop people with disabilities getting where they need to go.» Why are ramps important here? | They are only used for skating | They make parking spaces smaller | They hide the stone blocks | *They help people in wheelchairs get where they need to go
test: «Hedgehogs are getting rarer in Britain, so small things matter: a ramp in a pond.» Why might a ramp in a pond help a hedgehog? | *It gives the hedgehog a sloping way out of the water | It makes the water warmer | It makes the pond deeper | It stops the pond from freezing
exam: Which phrase uses ramp as a verb, meaning increase? | a skate ramp | *ramp up the speed | a wheelchair ramp | an on-ramp
